  "final_message": "The key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nHow the call works:\n- `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` in `audit.py`.\n- `write_audit` builds the key with `_format_key(kind, ident)` (`audit.py:11`).\n- `_format_key` returns `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`, and `AUDIT_PREFIX = \"AUD\"` comes from `config.py`.\n- So the key is `AUD` + `ORDER` + `7781`, joined with hyphens.\n\nThe key-building line in `audit.py` was hidden when I first printed the file. I checked it directly, and running `write_audit('order', '7781')` returned `{'AUD-ORDER-7781': True}`.\n\n`decoy_metrics.py` looks similar but writes `MET-...` keys to a metrics dict, not the audit log. `decoy_cache.py` doesn't touch the audit log either.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
